<title>USA: U.S. CASH SOYMEAL - BASIS OFFERS MOSTLY STEADY.</title>
<headline>U.S. CASH SOYMEAL - BASIS OFFERS MOSTLY STEADY.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis offers for rail and truck soymeal were mostly steady Wednesday, with the only strength at locations preparing for downtime.</p>
<p>Dealers said crushing plants at Danville, Ill., and Lafayette, Ind., were among those taking downtime next week.</p>
<p>The continued widening of the August/September premium on CBOT soymeal weighed on basis levels.</p>
<p>There was talk that at many locations there were cheaper protein source available for this month although soymeal should regain competitiveness in September.  </p>
